{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\n`examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md` teaches explicit bare assignees and offers direct status transition as an alternative to atomic claim. `examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md` describes an unsigned claimability fast-fail as a successful review cycle. Tickets [rebar:comely-craven-apatosaur] and [rebar:stealthful-calmy-erin] establish the enforced claim and review behavior. Ticket [rebar:arid-gutless-myna] introduced the inaccurate successful-cycle wording and requires an append-only correction. Dependency [rebar:helpful-stale-wildcat] established the portable identity rule in `templates/rebar-usage.md` and `templates/AGENTS.md`.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Replace every start-work alternative in the implementation skill with atomic `rebar claim <id>`. Atomic claim prevents two agents from claiming the same ticket.\n- Remove direct `rebar transition <id> open in_progress` as a start-work alternative.\n- Apply the identity rule from `templates/rebar-usage.md` and `templates/AGENTS.md`. Run claim without `--assignee`. A configured `ticket.default_assignee` applies that identity. An empty setting leaves the claimed ticket unassigned. Pass `--assignee` only for an explicit override. An override in a Jira-reconciled store must use email or accountId. Never prescribe a bare handle.\n- State in the brainstorm skill that blocked work defers plan review until it becomes claimable.\n- State that the claimability fast-fail returns unsigned `INDETERMINATE` with `coverage.llm_ran` set to false and exit status 2. This result is a deferral, not a successful review verdict.\n- Preserve dependency-order guidance and the prohibition on agent force.\n- Add a `rebar comment` to [rebar:arid-gutless-myna] that cites the enforced behavior. Do not edit its description or acceptance criteria, and do not reopen it.\n- Run focused skill frontmatter, synchronization, and workflow guidance checks.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The implementation skill requires atomic `rebar claim` for starting work.\n- [ ] The implementation skill no longer offers `rebar transition <id> open in_progress` as a start-work alternative.\n- [ ] The implementation skill presents claim without an explicit assignee as the default.\n- [ ] The implementation skill describes configured and empty `ticket.default_assignee` behavior.\n- [ ] Explicit override guidance requires email or accountId only for a Jira-reconciled store and never prescribes a bare handle.\n- [ ] The brainstorm skill defers review for blocked work until the ticket becomes claimable.\n- [ ] The brainstorm skill states that unsigned `INDETERMINATE` is not a successful verdict.\n- [ ] Both skills retain dependency-order guidance.\n- [ ] Both skills prohibit agent force.\n- [ ] [rebar:arid-gutless-myna] contains an append-only comment that cites the enforced behavior.\n- [ ] `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_agent_skill_ticket_workflow_guidance.py -q` passes.\n- [ ] Focused skill packaging and documentation checks pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787528709723369001,"uuid":"02de3698-8ba9-4fe0-a38f-1d874c95a2c3"}